abstract: >-
  A speculative hypothesis treating the universe as a globally conserved
  informational structure, where cosmological cycles correspond to changes in
  local information readability rather than temporal restarts. Version 0.2.0
  adds a conditional continuum field-detector and outcome-bearing tick study.
  Two retained-record marginals have distinct operator systems under a
  stipulated instrument, without establishing different generated algebras.
  An alternative instrument with the same POVM makes the second marginal
  field-independent. Selected detector identities and a conditional span lemma
  are Lean-checked, not the continuum independence argument or full dynamics.
  Earlier results and core postulates are unchanged. No physical algebra
  selector, cosmological entropy functional, transition dynamics, or prediction
  is derived. Reviews and diagnostic checks are internal and AI-assisted.
